{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph shows styles of music on a playlist. Country music songs are added to the playlist so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the songs are now Country. If the ratio of Hip Hop songs to Pop songs remains the same, what percentage of the total number of songs are now Hip Hop?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24fbeb4a686aa188bb86e1f1ef0aade379fa4c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; size(200);  usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;);  pen lightGray= rgb(&quot;b2afac&quot;); defaultpen(TimesRoman()); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7bp)); defaultpen(fontsize(13pt));  path Pop = (0,0) -- arc((0,0), 1, 0, 126) -- cycle; path Circle = arc((0,0), 1, 0, 360);  real cx = 1; real cy = -0.4; real s = 0.15;  draw(Circle); filldraw((cx,cy)--(cx+s,cy)--(cx+s,cy-s)--(cx,cy-s)--cycle, lightGray);  draw((cx,cy-0.23)--(cx+s,cy-0.23)--(cx+s,cy-s-0.23)--(cx,cy-0.15-0.23)--cycle); filldraw(Pop, lightGray);  label(&quot;$35\\%$&quot;, (0.5*cos(0.35*pi), 0.5*sin(0.35*pi))); label(&quot;Pop&quot;, (cx+1.5*s, cy-0.66*s), E); label(&quot;Hip Hop&quot;, (cx+1.5*s, cy-0.23-0.66*s), E); label(&quot;$65\\%$&quot;, (0.5*cos(-0.65*pi), 0.5*sin(-0.65*pi))); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"225\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Initially, the Hip Hop songs took up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e7328848cfea866a737a69554ca6e0efe6cb626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{35\\%}{35\\% + 65\\%} = 0.35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"151\" height=\"42\" /> of the combined total. After the Country songs are added, the Hip Hop and Pop songs will take up a combined total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f07e4b0f4a927535e85675d6ee651cd9644fbe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\% - 40\\$ = 60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" /> of the total number of songs, but the ratio between Hip Hop and Pop songs stays the same, so the Hip Hop songs take up the same proportion of that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7edd3842c40dbc1e54e522917a6e07b43c92e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, Hip Hop songs are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1d044539054ff053ed70841f02e3882c2f2a7d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.35 \\cdot 60\\% = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 39}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"167\" height=\"30\" /> percent of the total. \n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c49575f5cad3221167931cbba902de0a2b2fda21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> Pop songs and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae09190a559286693681f686f70903e861868d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> Hip Hop songs where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c49575f5cad3221167931cbba902de0a2b2fda21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae09190a559286693681f686f70903e861868d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are both whole numbers, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/02023709a6724dadb575788615352e9b35ef9530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> songs initially. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the number Country songs that are added. We are given that after the Country songs are added, they constitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the total number of songs. That is,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939567e1bdf458d4c7c265f73c4a2fd3cfca4269.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{C}{100k+C} = \\dfrac{2}{5} \\implies C = \\dfrac{2}{5}(100k + C) \\implies \\dfrac{3}{5}C = 40k \\implies  C = \\dfrac{200}{3}k\\]\" width=\"552\" height=\"38\" />\nThus, the percentage of Hip Hop songs is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f5f4d81f8b761ecf34abd54916c8f16fc31c39d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{65k}{100k + \\frac{200}{3}k} = \\frac{65}{100 + \\frac{200}{3}} = \\dfrac{65}{ \\frac{500}{3}} = 65 \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{500} = \\frac{39}{100} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 39\\%}\\]\" width=\"493\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"20